{
  "english_witnesses": [
    {
      "stem": "shacharit_elohai_netzor",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/elohai_netzor",
      "title": {
        "he": "אלהי נצור",
        "en": "My God, guard my tongue"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s123",
                "printed_page": "47",
                "text": "My God, guard my tongue from evil and my lips from speaking falsehood. Towards those who curse me, let my soul be silent and let my soul be as dust in relation to everything. Open my heart to Thy Torah and let my soul pursue Thy commandments and as for all those that devise evil against",
                "page_start": false
              },
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "me, speedily frustrate their counsel and upset their plan. Do this for the sake of Thy Name, do this for the sake of Thy right hand, do this for the sake of Thy holiness, do this for the sake of Thy Torah",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/elohai_netzor/text",
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/elohai_netzor"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "so that those who love Thee may be delivered. Save with Thy right hand and respond to me.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/60/7",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/60/7",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/elohai_netzor/quotations/quoted_psalms_60_7/7",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/elohai_netzor/quotations/quoted_psalms_60_7"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "May the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart find favour before Thee, O Lord, my Rock and my Redeemer.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/19/15",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/19/15",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/elohai_netzor/quotations/quoted_psalms_19_15/15",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/elohai_netzor/quotations/quoted_psalms_19_15"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "May He who makes peace in His heights, make peace for us and for all Israel, and say, Amen.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/elohai_netzor"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "shacharit_yehi_ratzon_temple",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/yehi_ratzon_temple",
      "title": {
        "he": "יהי רצון — בנין המקדש",
        "en": "Restoration of the Temple"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "May it find favour before Thee, O Lord our God and God of our fathers, that the sanctuary be rebuilt speedily in our days, and grant our portion in Thy Torah. There we will serve Thee in awe as in the days of old and former years.",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/yehi_ratzon_temple/text",
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/yehi_ratzon"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "And pleasant unto the Lord shall be the offering of Judah and Jerusalem as in the days of old and former years.",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:malachi/3/4",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:malachi/3/4",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/yehi_ratzon_temple/quotations/quoted_malachi_3_4/4",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/yehi_ratzon_temple/quotations/quoted_malachi_3_4"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "repetition_avot_open",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/avot/open",
      "title": {
        "he": "ברכת אבות — פתיחה",
        "en": "ברכת אבות — פתיחה"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God and God of our fathers, God of Abraham, God of Isaac and God of Jacob, great, mighty and awe-inspiring God, God the Most High, who performs acts of kindness and owns everything and remembers the good deeds of the fathers and will bring a redeemer for their children’s children for His Name’s sake in love.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/avot/open/text",
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/avot/barukh_attah"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "misod_chakhamim",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:misod_chakhamim",
      "title": {
        "he": "מִסּוֹד חֲכָמִים",
        "en": "מִסּוֹד חֲכָמִים"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "Choosing from the counsel of wise and discerning men and from the teaching of those that understand knowledge, I open my mouth in prayer and supplication to entreat and implore the countenance of the King of Kings and the Lord of Lords.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:misod_chakhamim/text"
          }
        ]
      },
      "citations": {
        "he": [
          {
            "scan": "s124",
            "text": "(נ״א פני ממ״ה מלא רחמים)",
            "note_type": "commentary",
            "target": "#misod_variant"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "et_chil_yom_pequddah",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:et_chil_yom_pequddah",
      "title": {
        "he": "אֶת חִיל יוֹם פקודה",
        "en": "אֶת חִיל יוֹם פקודה"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s125",
                "printed_page": "48",
                "text": "The fearful day of reckoning has arrived. All flesh is full of dread of reprimand. They approach to bend the knee before Him, to purify their thoughts as in the flame of the altar. He who has formed the heart of all of them together, judges so that rich and poor alike are judged according to the scales. He remembers him who said: ‘Will He not do justice?’ His valued prayer will be recalled in judgment. Before He formed any creature, he had planned that rock from which we were hewn (Abraham). Central between past and future",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/et_chil_yom_pequddah/part_1"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 2,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s127",
                "printed_page": "49",
                "text": "was he hewn, on him the whole structure is founded. His allotted wife was on this day granted vigour to bring forth a shoot at ninety years. She was set as an example for the roselike nation to appear before God at this beginning of the year. Her children tremble on this day while they stand before the awe-inspiring throne. They let their prayers be heard this day. They blow with a loud blast to find salvation. On her (Sarah) do they rely, to be considered for her sake, they cry out in assembly, knock at the gates, depend on the ashes of the sheep at the sacrifice of Isaac, the glorious gift with which she had been considered.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/et_chil_yom_pequddah/part_2"
          }
        ]
      },
      "citations": {
        "he": [
          {
            "scan": "s126",
            "text": "(נ״א כחֻק)",
            "note_type": "commentary",
            "target": "#et_chil_variant"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
